o":"nothing","termine_origine":"والو","termine_origine_traslitterazione":"wālu","catena":[{"codice":"ary","nome":"Moroccan Arabic","termine":"والو","traslitterazione":"wālu","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"ary","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Moroccan Arabic والو (wālu)."},{"parola":"wesh","pos":"intj|noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"Stresses or emphasizes a fact or event.","termine_origine":"واش","termine_origine_traslitterazione":"wāš","catena":[{"codice":"ary","nome":"Moroccan Arabic","termine":"واش","traslitterazione":"wāš","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"arq","nome":"Algerian Arabic","termine":"واش راك","traslitterazione":"wāš rāk","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"arq","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Many etymologies have been proposed. The leading theories find its roots in Maghrebi Arabic varieties, primarily from Moroccan Arabic واش (wāš, an interrogative particle), or through ellipsis of Algerian Arabic واش راك (wāš rāk, “what's up?”); in Moroccan Arabic, interrogatives شنو (šnu) and آش (ʔāš"}]}